# Every route that the flash-web server passes on to flash-be, one request each, plus what it refuses before it asks
# the API. The routes and the replies are in docs/reference/http-endpoints.md; the demo story is api-flash-demo.http.
#
# Before you start: `npm run demo:setup`, then `npm run demo:dev` (the API and the web server).
#
# The format is kulala.nvim (https://github.com/wahidyankf/kulala.nvim). A request named with `# @name` keeps its
# reply: send "the current sale", "join the queue" and "hold one item" before the requests that use them. The Shared
# block attaches kulala's cookie jar to every request, and the web server passes the cookies on. It refuses a POST
# whose Origin is another site.

### Shared
# @attach-cookie-jar
@web = http://localhost:3000

### Health of the web server itself (no call to the API)
GET {{web}}/api/health

### Sign up as a shopper (201 and the two cookies; the refresh cookie comes back for /api/v1/auth, the path the browser calls)
POST {{web}}/api/v1/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "shopper-web", "password": "a long password" }

### Log in (when sign-up answers 409 username_taken)
POST {{web}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "shopper-web", "password": "a long password" }

### Who am I?
GET {{web}}/api/v1/auth/me

### The current sale (what the page reads)
# @name current
GET {{web}}/api/v1/sales/current

### One sale by id
GET {{web}}/api/v1/sales/{{current.response.body.$.id}}

### Join the queue
# @name join
POST {{web}}/api/v1/sales/{{current.response.body.$.id}}/queue

### Check your place (waiting, admitted or absent; the delay lets one admission tick pass)
# @delay 1500
GET {{web}}/api/v1/sales/{{current.response.body.$.id}}/queue/me
x-queue-ticket: {{join.response.body.$.ticket}}

### Hold one item
# @name reserve
POST {{web}}/api/v1/sales/{{current.response.body.$.id}}/reservations
x-queue-ticket: {{join.response.body.$.ticket}}

### Pay for the held item
POST {{web}}/api/v1/sales/{{current.response.body.$.id}}/purchases
Content-Type: application/json

{ "reservationId": "{{reserve.response.body.$.reservationId}}" }

### Did I get it?
GET {{web}}/api/v1/sales/{{current.response.body.$.id}}/purchases/me

### Live sale status (Server-Sent Events, streamed through the web server; closes after 5 seconds here)
# @accept chunked
# @curl-max-time 5
GET {{web}}/api/v1/sales/{{current.response.body.$.id}}/events

### Live place in the queue (closes after 5 seconds here)
# @accept chunked
# @curl-max-time 5
GET {{web}}/api/v1/sales/{{current.response.body.$.id}}/queue/me/events
x-queue-ticket: {{join.response.body.$.ticket}}

### Renew the login
POST {{web}}/api/v1/auth/refresh

### Log out
POST {{web}}/api/v1/auth/logout

###############################################################################
# What the web server refuses before it asks the API.
###############################################################################

### A path that is not on the list: 404 not_found
GET {{web}}/api/v1/sales/current/secret

### A sale id that is not a UUID: 404 not_found
GET {{web}}/api/v1/sales/not-a-uuid

### A POST from another site: 403 cross_site
POST {{web}}/api/v1/auth/login
Origin: http://evil.example
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "shopper-web", "password": "a long password" }

### An old path without the version: 404 not_found (every API route is under /api/v1)
GET {{web}}/api/sales/current

### The operator routes are never passed on: 404 not_found (manage sales on the API, see api-flash-be.http)
GET {{web}}/api/v1/admin/sales
